<meta type=article title="Static ABC rendering (DSL Slice 2)">
</meta>

<section | Build-time notation>

In static mode the abc handler's contract markup is replaced, at compile
time, by inline SVG. The page that opens this document needs no abcjs
bundle and no init script: the notation is already drawn. This is the
build-time path that live mode and the `<pre>` contract (RQ-DSL-M2) set up.

<abc #music:c-scale>
X:1
T:C Major Scale
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
C D E F | G A B c |
</abc>

A second excerpt with no id confirms the emit path handles both the
id-bearing and the anonymous contract: the renderer runs on each marked
block, and only the id-bearing one carries an id onto its `<svg>`.

<abc>
X:1
T:Short Phrase
M:3/4
L:1/4
K:G
G2 A | B2 c | d3 |
</abc>

Surrounding prose continues to render normally — the replacement is scoped
to the abc contract elements and leaves everything else untouched.
